# uv.lock is committed. If CI re-resolved dependencies every run, the build could suddenly
# break even though nothing changed on our side

# Data layer: raw is immutable, append-only, and committed (design note, principle 1)
# Negate the *.gz exclusion for the raw layer only. *.db (DuckDB) is a build artifact and stays ignored
!data/raw/**/*.json.gz
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
target/
dbt_packages/
logs/

# The anonymous usage ID generated by dbt
.user.yml

# The mart layer is a build artifact. It can be reproduced from raw and models, and
# fct_observations.csv alone is 12MB, so committing it daily would bloat the repository.
# raw (immutable, around 1MB) and the transformation logic are committed, so reproducibility holds
data/mart/

# workspace
*.code-workspace

# Claude
CLAUDE.md